{
  "name": "history-range-transition-first",
  "description": "A calendar-year definition that changes to 1 April years through a three-month transition 0002-01-01 to 0002-03-31. Regime 0 has no fiscal year in the supported range: its year 0001 starts on 0001-01-01, before 0001-01-02. So the transition is the first supported fiscal year (number 2 by 'end'; 'start' would give the transition and the year after it the same number 2), and year 1, years from 1 or 0, shift before the transition, locate on 0001-12-31 and a dimension that starts there are OUT_OF_RANGE. Illustrative.",
  "source": {
    "kind": "oracle",
    "citation": "Independent implementation of the spec in conformance/generators/fiscal_oracle.py, written with Python datetime and no fiscalclock code",
    "url": null,
    "checked_by": "fiscal_oracle.py: Calendar.seq built from the regimes and transitions; change_errors and naming_errors pass"
  },
